#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:1
msgid "Release process"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:3
msgid ""
"_Black_'s release process has been standardized and automated. This document "
"explains what to expect and how to release _Black_ using said automation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:6
msgid "Release cadence"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:8
msgid ""
"**We aim to release whatever is on `main` every 1-2 months.** This ensures "
"merged improvements and bugfixes are shipped to users reasonably quickly, "
"while not massively fracturing the userbase with too many versions. This "
"also keeps the workload on maintainers consistent and predictable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:13
msgid ""
"If there's not much new on `main` to justify a release, it's acceptable to "
"skip a month's release. Ideally January releases should not be skipped, "
"since the first release in a new calendar year may make changes to the "
"_stable_ style, as per our [stability policy](labels/stability-policy). "
"While the policy applies to the first release (instead of only January "
"releases), confining changes to the stable style to January will keep things "
"predictable (and nicer) for users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:20
msgid ""
"Unless there is a serious regression or bug that requires immediate "
"patching, **there should not be more than one release per month**. While "
"version numbers are cheap, releases require a maintainer to commit not only "
"to the actual cutting of a release, but also to deal with the potential "
"fallout post-release. Releasing more frequently than monthly nets rapidly "
"diminishing returns."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:26
msgid "Cutting a release"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:28
msgid ""
"**You must have `write` permissions for the _Black_ repository to cut a "
"release.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:30
msgid ""
"The 10,000-foot view of the release process is that you trigger a workflow "
"to create a PR automating the release chores. Then, merge it, triggering "
"[release automation](#release-workflows) that builds all release artifacts "
"and publishes them to the various platforms we publish to."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:35
msgid ""
"Start here for prereleases as well. Run \"prepare release\" against `main` "
"as described before stabilizing preview features or making other prerelease "
"changes. The appropriate times to do those are included in the instructions "
"below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:39
msgid "To cut a release:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:41
msgid ""
"**Run [the \"prepare release\" workflow][prepare-release-workflow].** Make "
"sure to leave the main branch selected. This will create a PR automating "
"most of the needed changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:44
msgid ""
"For stable versions, the workflow will automatically determine the next "
"version number. Leave the `Version_Override` input empty."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:46
msgid ""
"For reference, _Black_ follows the [CalVer] versioning standard using the "
"`YY.M.N` format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:48
msgid ""
"Unless there already has been a release during the month, `N` should be `0`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:49
msgid "Example: the first release in January 2026 is `26.1.0`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:50
msgid ""
"If you're releasing a prerelease, specify **the expected stable release "
"version** in the box provided (not the version of the prerelease). The "
"prerelease version will be determined automatically, following these rules:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:53
msgid "Prereleases use the `YY.MMaN` format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:54
msgid "The first alpha should start `N` at `1` (not `0`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:55
msgid ""
"Example: the first alpha released in December 2025 and to be stabilized in "
"January 2026 is `26.1a1`, but `Version_Override` should be set to `26.1.0`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:58
msgid ""
"You will be auto-assigned to the created PR. **Check the changelog diff in "
"the description and copyedit `CHANGES.md`.** The CI will update it after "
"each push, so double-check it again before you merge. Things to check "
"include:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:61
msgid ""
"Make sure nothing was put into the wrong version or section, particularly "
"things that you might want to move to \"Highlights\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:63
msgid ""
"Rephrase unclear or unnecessarily detailed entries (a sentence or two is "
"probably plenty for most changes)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:65
msgid "Remove duplicates, fix typos, and reorder entries if needed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:67
msgid ""
"**If you're releasing a prerelease or major version, commit the changes "
"unique to it** to the PR branch. If you make any changes that should have a "
"changelog entry, remember to add one!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:71
msgid ""
"If you're releasing a major version (or a prerelease for one), there are "
"some specific additional changes to make at this point:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:73
msgid ""
"Bump `wcwidth` to the latest version and run `scripts/make_width_table.py`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:74
msgid ""
"Find any references to the old version and bump them (references to minor "
"versions are auto-bumped, so you don't need to check when releasing minor "
"versions)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:77
msgid "**Wait for CI to pass on the PR, and fix any failures.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:78
msgid ""
"If CI does not pass, **stop** and investigate the failure(s) as we'd "
"generally want to fix failing CI before cutting a release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:81
msgid ""
"**To cut a stable release, merge the PR once everything looks good.** If "
"you're cutting a prerelease, **do not merge it**, and instead [run the \"cut "
"release\" workflow][cut-release-workflow] manually. **Make sure to select "
"the `ci/prepare-release/<verson>` branch**, where `<version>` is the stable "
"version you're preparing. You can release multiple prereleases from the same "
"PR by running \"cut release\" multiple times after any desired changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:88
msgid ""
"**Make sure CI passes.** At this point, you're basically done, but it's good "
"practice to [watch and verify that all the release workflows pass][black-"
"actions], though GitHub may notify you anyway if something fails."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:91
msgid ""
"If something fails, don't panic. Please go read the respective workflow's "
"logs and configuration file to reverse-engineer your way to a solution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:93
msgid ""
"If the failure is in the \"cut release\" workflow before \"update stable\" "
"runs, you're able to commit a fix to `main` and rerun it manually with no "
"issues. Again, run it on the `main` branch for stable releases or the `ci/"
"prepare-release/<verson>` branch for prereleases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:97
msgid ""
"If a different workflow fails, the release can't be fully reverted at this "
"point. Determine the best course of action according to what failed and the "
"necessary changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:100
msgid ""
"After a stable release is published, the CI will also create a PR to add the "
"next version's changelog. Once everything passes, merge it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:103
msgid ""
"Congratulations! You've successfully cut a new release of _Black_. Go stand "
"up and take a break, you deserve it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:107
msgid ""
"Once the release artifacts are published, you may see new issues being filed "
"indicating regressions. While regressions are not great, they don't "
"automatically mean a hotfix release is warranted. Unless the regressions are "
"serious and impact many users, a hotfix release is probably unnecessary. In "
"the end, use your best judgment and ask other maintainers for their thoughts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:114
msgid "Release workflows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:116
msgid ""
"All of _Black_'s release automation uses [GitHub Actions]. All workflows are "
"therefore configured using YAML files in the `.github/workflows` directory "
"of the _Black_ repository. They are triggered at various points in the "
"release process detailed above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:120
msgid "prepare release"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:122
msgid ""
"This workflow is manually run as the first step in the release process. It "
"handles many of the initial chores before releasing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:125
msgid "create"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:127
msgid ""
"This job runs `scripts/release.py` to clean up CHANGES.md and bump most "
"references to old _Black_ versions, then creates a PR with the changes for "
"your review. The PR creation is authenticated in order to trigger test CI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:132
#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:169
#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:180
msgid ""
"_Currently this workflow uses a GitHub API token associated with "
"@JelleZijlstra's account._"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:136
msgid "update"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:138
msgid ""
"This job runs after `create` and after each subsequent push to the PR. It "
"updates the changelog diff in the PR description."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:141
msgid "cut release"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:143
msgid ""
"This workflow runs when the changelog PR is merged (or when manually "
"triggered, in the case of prereleases or reruns after a failure). It creates "
"and publishes a release, which triggers the other release workflows, then "
"completes final post-release chores."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:147
msgid "release"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:149
msgid ""
"This job determines if the release should be a prerelease (if the workflow "
"is run on a branch other than `main`). It then creates a draft release for "
"the next step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:152
msgid "build-binaries (…)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:154
msgid ""
"These matrix jobs build native executables for multiple platforms using "
"[PyInstaller]. This allows people to download the executable for their "
"platform and run _Black_ without a Python runtime installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:158
msgid ""
"The created binaries are stored on the associated draft GitHub Release for "
"download. Note that we use [GitHub's immutable releases][immutable-"
"releases], preventing assets or tags from being modified once the release is "
"published as a security measure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:162
msgid "update-stable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:164
msgid ""
"This job marks the release as published. This is authenticated in order to "
"trigger further release automation. Then, only if the release was stable, it "
"updates the `stable` branch by force pushing it to the most recent tag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:173
msgid "new-changelog"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:175
msgid ""
"This job opens a new PR to add the \"Unreleased\" section back to the "
"changelog. The PR is not auto-merged to allow the releaser time to make sure "
"all the release workflows succeed. The PR creation is authenticated in order "
"to trigger test CI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:184
msgid "build and publish"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:186
msgid ""
"This is our main workflow, triggered when the release is published. It "
"builds an [sdist] and [wheels] to upload to PyPI, where the vast majority of "
"users download _Black_ from."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:189
msgid ""
"It also runs as a test dry run on each PR and push to `main` (without "
"publishing anything to PyPI)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:192
msgid "sdist + pure wheel"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:194
msgid ""
"This single job builds the sdist and pure Python wheel (i.e., a wheel that "
"only contains Python code) using [Hatch]. These artifacts are general-"
"purpose and can be used on basically any platform supported by Python."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:198
msgid "generate wheels matrix / mypyc wheels (…)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:200
msgid ""
"We use [mypyc] to compile _Black_ into a CPython C extension for "
"significantly improved performance. Wheels built with mypyc are platform and "
"Python version specific. [Supported platforms are documented in the FAQ]"
"(labels/mypyc-support)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:204
msgid ""
"These matrix jobs use [cibuildwheel] which handles the complicated task of "
"building C extensions for many environments for us. It uses a matrix to "
"build each platform in parallel (as noted in the job name in parentheses)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:208
msgid "publish-hatch / publish-mypyc"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:210
msgid ""
"These jobs upload the built sdist and all wheels to PyPI using [Trusted "
"Publishing]. This step does not run on PRs or pushes to `main`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:213
msgid "docker"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:215
msgid ""
"This workflow uses Docker Buildx to build and push `arm64` and `amd64`/"
"`x86_64` builds of the official _Black_ Docker image to Docker Hub."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:218
msgid "This also runs on each push to `main`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/release_process.md:221
msgid ""
"_Currently this workflow uses a Docker API token associated with "
"@cooperlees's account._"
msgstr ""
